Finally, after twelve years of off-and-on trying (mostly off...), I
made it!

A convenient altar on lvl1 kept me out of trouble in the early game.
On lvl11 I found another altar in a nice isolated location, converted
it, and made it my stash location using a wand of fire I found in
Sokoban.  From there, the quest, Fort Ludios, Medusa, and the Castle
easily fell.  I found a silver dragon on Ludios, which left me some
convenient scales and led to an odd Val armor combo: SDSM-CoMR-"oLS.

Major plusses:
- found 3 "oLS (saved my life twice)
- found 3 bags of holding
- learned some monster strategy (teleport to up-stair to heal) and used
the knowledge to take out the quest nemesis and named demons
- Orb of Fate showed me all the elemental portals without needing a
recharge (I didn't have any scrolls of charging left!)
- Found the right altar on the first try, and it was guarded by Famine
(pushover!)

Major stupid mistakes for a first-time ascender:
- Ate a chameleon corpse (lost first CoMR and an enchanted T-shirt)
- Recited a couple of enchant armor scrolls without checking (cursed of
course)
- Dropped 2 potions of gain level on an altar--while levitating
(peculiar odor indeed)
- Lost an "oLS to choking (Didn't read the stop eating question
carefully)
- Melee'd Rodney and the High Priest of Moloch rather than breaking out
the wand o' death (lost another "oLS here)
- Carried too much in a blessed BoH, which Rodney promptly cursed
(Overtaxed!)
- Forgot to copy the Astral map because I was too excited

Thanks to RGRN and WikiHack for having all the answers to my strategy
questions :)

